%erg 0.1
Title: sync: isolate every untrusted fetch, honour adopter insteadOf, degrade gracefully
Created: 2026-09-17
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-09-17T10:19Z haduong created

--- body ---

## Context

Post-merge review of PR #371 (ticket 0301), all findings measured:
https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg/pull/371#pullrequestreview-5234047880

- Medium: the throwaway bare repo has an empty config, so a repo-local
  `url.<mirror>.insteadOf` for the hardcoded upstream URL is bypassed and the
  adopter silently receives github.com bytes instead of its pinned mirror.
- Medium: isolation is gated on `shallow`, so a configured source
  (`ERG_UPDATE_URL` / `.ergrc [update]`) still fetches unshallow straight into
  the adopter's object store -- the #370 defect class in the arm not probed.
- Low: `MkdirTemp` / `init --bare` failures return `unavailable: false`, so a
  read-only or full ticket store exits 1 against the documented exit-0 contract.
- Low: the explicit `RemoveAll` after `cat-file` turns a successful fetch into
  exit 1 when cleanup fails; the `defer` already cleans up.
- Low: `.erg-sync-*` lives inside the adopter's work tree; a signal during the
  fetch leaks it and a concurrent `git add -A` would commit a bare repo.
- Nit: 0301 closed with all six exit criteria unticked.
- Nit: the "Linux x86-64 traveler" wording finding from #370 was never disposed.

## Exit criteria

- [x] the fetch URL is resolved in the adopter's repository
      (`git ls-remote --get-url`) before the throwaway repo is created, so
      repo-local `insteadOf` is honoured; the resolved URL never reaches a
      message unsanitized; a fixture with the redirect in `.git/config` (not
      `GIT_CONFIG_*`) is red on the base and green after
- [x] every source except the trusted project origin fetches in the throwaway
      repo; a configured-source fixture proves no object import and no
      `FETCH_HEAD` in the adopter repo, red on the base
- [x] temp-dir creation or `init --bare` failure exits 0 with the binary
      untouched (`unavailable: true`); fixture on a read-only store
- [x] a cleanup failure after a successful `cat-file` returns the bytes and at
      most warns on stderr
- [x] `cmdSync` sweeps stale `.erg-sync-*` directories at start; `erg check`
      and `erg validate` ignore that directory
- [x] help text and `docs/erg-manual.md` describe the new confinement, and
      `AGENTS.md`'s confinement claim is true of `sync` as a whole
- [x] 0301's exit criteria are ticked or annotated, and its log disposes of the
      x86-64 wording nit (deferred: sniff the fetched bytes, no ticket until a
      non-Linux adopter with a vendored native erg exists)
- [x] `make test`, `make validate`, ticket DAG pass
